@startuml
' High-level class diagram for StopwatchService with periodic timer

class StopwatchService {
    +start()
    +pause()
    +stop()
    +recordLap()
    +dispose()
    +stream : Stream<StopwatchStateEntity>
    +laps : List<LapEntity>
    -_tickPeriodInMs: int
    -_timerSubscription: StreamSubscription<int>?
}

class LapEntity {
    +index: int
    +lapTime: int
}

class StopwatchStateEntity {
    +elapsedTimeInMs: int
    +laps: List<LapEntity>
    +isComplete: bool
}

StopwatchService "1" --> "*" LapEntity : records
StopwatchService "1" --> "1" StopwatchStateEntity : emits state

' Periodic timer represented as an associated concept
class StreamPeriodicTimer {
    +listen(callback: Function)
}

StopwatchService "1" --> "1" StreamPeriodicTimer : uses for ticks

note right of StreamPeriodicTimer
  Periodically emits tick events every _tickPeriodInMs milliseconds.
  Each tick triggers the _tick() method in StopwatchService,
  which updates elapsed time and emits a new StopwatchStateEntity.
end note

@enduml
